# The single configuration file for every connector under .system/connectors/.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# Copy this to `.env` and fill in the keys you use. This file is the example;
# `.env` is the real one and must never be committed or shared.
#
# RULES
#
# 1. Every variable MUST carry its connector's prefix -- GRANOLA_, SLACK_,
#    OPENAI_. This is not cosmetic. Each connector's wrapper exports ONLY the
#    variables matching its own prefix, so a bug or a bad npm dependency in one
#    connector never sees another connector's credentials. An unprefixed
#    variable is invisible to every connector.
#
# 2. Prefixes must be unique per connector. Two connectors sharing one prefix
#    share their secrets, silently.
#
# 3. Secrets and options live together here, separated by prefix rather than by
#    file. Keep each connector's block contiguous and commented.
#
# This file lives in `.system/`, which Obsidian ignores and Obsidian Sync skips
# -- so it does NOT travel between machines. That is deliberate: re-create it on
# each machine. Git and Google Drive do NOT skip dotfolders; keep this file out
# of both.

# --- granola-export ---------------------------------------------------------
# Secret. Granola desktop app: Settings -> Connectors -> API keys
# (Business/Enterprise plan required). Scope: "Personal notes".
GRANOLA_API_KEY=grn_paste_your_key_here

# Options. All optional; the connector runs on its defaults without them.
#
# Write somewhere other than <vault>/Resources/Meetings. Year subfolders are
# created beneath whatever base you give. On Windows write the path literally,
# no escaping: GRANOLA_OUT_DIR=C:\path\to\vault\Resources\Meetings
# GRANOLA_OUT_DIR=/absolute/path/to/vault/Resources/Meetings
#
# Include full transcripts (slower, larger files).
# GRANOLA_TRANSCRIPT=1
#
# Cap export.log at the last n runs (default 1000).
# GRANOLA_LOG_KEEP_RUNS=1000
